That is a much cleaner UX approach. A scrollable box inside a modal can sometimes feel cramped, whereas a "Show More" / "Show Less" toggle feels modern and keeps the interface looking light.
Here is how to implement the expanding description text.
### 1. Add the State Variable
First, add a new state variable near the top of your JournalAuthorization.jsx file (right around line 160 where your other useState hooks are):
```javascript
  const [isDescExpanded, setIsDescExpanded] = useState(false);

```
### 2. Reset the State on Close
To ensure the description doesn't stay expanded when you open a different batch, reset the state inside your handleCloseViewModal function:
```javascript
  const handleCloseViewModal = () => {
    setIsViewModalOpen(false);
    setBatchDetails([]);
    setViewingBatchId(null);
    setViewingBatchCreatorId(null);
    setIsDescExpanded(false); // Reset the expansion state
    fetchPendingBatches();
  };

```
### 3. Update the Description UI
Scroll down to the View Details Modal. Find the Grid item for the **Description** (inside SECTION 1: VOUCHER ORIGIN DETAILS) and replace it completely with this code:
```javascript
                        {/* --- EXPANDABLE DESCRIPTION --- */}
                        <Grid item xs={12}>
                          <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" display="block" gutterBottom>
                            Description
                          </Typography>
                          <Box sx={{ 
                            backgroundColor: '#ffffff', 
                            border: '1px solid #cbd5e1', 
                            borderRadius: 1, 
                            p: 1.5 
                          }}>
                            <Typography variant="body2" color="text.primary" sx={{ whiteSpace: "pre-wrap", lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
                              {vidDetails.DESCRIPTION 
                                ? (isDescExpanded || vidDetails.DESCRIPTION.length <= 150 
                                    ? vidDetails.DESCRIPTION 
                                    : `${vidDetails.DESCRIPTION.substring(0, 150)}...`) 
                                : "No description provided."}
                            </Typography>
                            
                            {/* Only show the toggle button if the text is longer than 150 characters */}
                            {vidDetails.DESCRIPTION && vidDetails.DESCRIPTION.length > 150 && (
                              <Box sx={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'flex-end', mt: 0.5 }}>
                                <Button 
                                  size="small" 
                                  onClick={() => setIsDescExpanded(!isDescExpanded)}
                                  sx={{ textTransform: 'none', p: 0, minWidth: 'auto', fontWeight: 'bold' }}
                                >
                                  {isDescExpanded ? "Show Less" : "Show More"}
                                </Button>
                              </Box>
                            )}
                          </Box>
                        </Grid>

```
### How this works:
 * It checks if the text is longer than 150 characters.
 * If it is short, it just displays the text normally with no button.
 * If it is long, it cuts it off at 150 characters and adds ... at the end, placing a neat **"Show More"** button underneath.
 * Clicking the button expands the text to full height instantly and changes the button to **"Show Less"**.
